                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Played On: [b]HTC Vive[/b][/h1]\n\nIf you're low on cash and needing a fix of VR shooting, then look no further than RAYGUN COMMANDO, an on-rails, stage-based sci-fi shooter that lasts roughly 15 minutes per complete playthrough. There's no story, but you pretty much just have to defend your spaceship from the onslaught of invaders that are trying to board it. You get one gun and infinite ammo, though you do have to keep reloading, and once you've dealt with all of the enemies on one stage, you're instantly transported to the next.\n\nWhat the game lacks in aesthetic variety between stages, it makes up for with a decent soundtrack and genuinely fun gameplay. There are only a few different enemy models, but there's also a boss battle near the end of the game. Not to mention, there are actually zero-g physics during a couple stages. There is no locomotion, so you must dodge incoming attacks or deflect projectiles with your gun. If you get tired of arcade mode, there's even a 2 minute time attack mode.\n\nRAYGUN COMMANDO is as good as it gets when it comes down to a free shooting title. The developer is still active in the forums, and although the game released in January 2017, there was an update as recently as August 2017 at the time of writing. This title shows clear love from its developer, and hopefully in the future we will see some amazing paid content that elaborates on their game creating skills, but for that to happen more enemy and location diversity would be essential, as well as a longer campaign mode. Keep up the great work!\n\n[h1]Rating: [b]4.0/5.0[/b] - Excellent, highly worth playing.[/h1]\nThe VR Network [url=https://store.steampowered.com/curator/33182845-The-VR-Network/]Curator[/url] | [url=https://steamcommunity.com/groups/thevrnetwork]Group[/url] Click for More",
